{
  "borough": "London Borough of Barking and Dagenham",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The standard of accommodation, particularly the size and dimensions of the proposed bedrooms and overall layout of the unit is unacceptable. The bedrooms are small and narrow. The development&nbsp;fails to provide high-quality, accessible accommodation, particularly noting the unit is presented as a family-sized unit. The lack of windows to the living and kitchen space will result in a loss of daylight and ventilation which will have a negative impact the quality of life and living standards for current and future residents. . Overall, the proposal does not present a high standard of accommodation. The proposal is therefore considered to be contrary to:Policy D6 of the London Plan (March 2021);Policy CC1 of the Core Strategy DPD (July 2010);Policies BC4 and BP5 of the Borough Wide Development Policy DPD (March 2011);Policies SP 3 and DMD 1 of the London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Draft Local Plan 2037 (Regulation 19 Submission Version, December 2021)",
    "The proposed development by reason of its scale, mass, bulk and siting would generate a harmful loss of amenity, particularly to no.38 Buller Road. It will result in a loss of daylight, sunlight and overshadowing to the amenity space and habitable rooms which officers consider to be unneighbourly. The proposal is therefore considered to be contrary to:Paragraph 132 of the National Planning Policy Framework (2023)Policy D6 of the London Plan (March 2021)Policy CP3 of the Core Strategy DPD (July 2010)Policy BP8 of the Borough Wide Development Plan Document (March 2011)Policy DMD1 of the London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Draft Local Plan 2037 (Regulation 19 Submission Version, December 2021)."
  ],
